Subject: [PATCH] Keep produced outputs in the local CAS instead of the content store

Base: facebook/buck2 9a1876786f32806f6b65fc51f4c1c3077efc38a5 plus the
preceding Sekka patches.

On the CAS host with cache writes (BUCK2_LOCAL_CAS_DIR and
BUCK2_LOCAL_CAS_JOURNAL), every produced output is uploaded to the CAS
anyway, so ingesting it into the content store as well only repeats the
work: a verified canonical stage and syncs per file under the exclusive
lock, which four worktrees rebuilding at once queued on (88 s each, in
lockstep). Produced outputs now skip ingestion; after the cache uploader
finishes, it appends one HASH SIZE PATH line per output file to the
journal, and the client shares those files' extents with their CAS blobs
after the build. The journal joins the daemon startup identity. Read-only
clients and hosts without a local CAS are unchanged.

